@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}
<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>

<p>
    This policy explains how TimeTracker handles information when you use this application.
    It applies to this TimeTracker deployment; the organization that operates it is responsible
    for its configuration and for responding to privacy requests.
</p>

<h2>Information this application handles</h2>
<ul>
    <li>
        <strong>Account information:</strong> your sign-in name, supplied by the hosting
        platform's authentication service, is used to identify your account and determine
        whether you are authorized to use the application.
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Time-tracking information:</strong> customer and project names, and the start
        and end times of tracked work. These names and records may contain information about
        people or businesses if you choose to include it.
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Session information:</strong> the application uses a session cookie to support
        features such as remembering your last selected project. The session expires after
        30 minutes of inactivity.
    </li>
</ul>

<h2>How information is used</h2>
<p>
    Information is used to provide time tracking, display and export reports, associate records
    with your account, and operate and protect the application. The application scopes customer,
    project, and time-entry records to the account configured for you.
</p>

<h2>Storage and sharing</h2>
<p>
    Account and time-tracking records are stored in the database configured for this deployment.
    The application does not include advertising or analytics features. The organization
    operating the application and its hosting, authentication, and database providers may process
    information as needed to provide and maintain the service. The operator controls the
    deployment, including where data is hosted and which providers are used.
</p>

<h2>Retention and your choices</h2>
<p>
    Records remain in the deployment's database until they are deleted by an authorized
    administrator or according to the operator's retention practices. Contact your organization's
    TimeTracker administrator to request access to, correction of, or deletion of information,
    or to ask how long it is retained. You can end your application session by closing your
    browser; this does not delete stored records.
</p>

<h2>Security</h2>
<p>
    Access is limited to accounts configured by the operator, and the application separates
    records by account. No internet service can guarantee absolute security. Use only information
    you are authorized to enter and avoid adding sensitive personal information unless your
    organization has approved its use here.
</p>

<h2>Changes and contact</h2>
<p>
    The operator may update this policy when the application or its practices change. For
    questions about this deployment or this policy, contact your organization's TimeTracker
    administrator.
</p>
